<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<model>
  <name>Traffic Light</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>LIMO curriculum</name>
  </author>
  <description>
    3-lens traffic pole (red/yellow/green), one Gazebo link per lens
    (red_light_link / yellow_light_link / green_light_link).

    Color is controlled at runtime via the traffic_light_plugin model
    plugin (limo_plugin package), by publishing std_msgs/String on
    /traffic_light/color:

      ros2 topic pub -1 /traffic_light/color std_msgs/msg/String "{data: 'green'}"

    Valid values: red, yellow, green, off.

    We originally tried the standard gazebo_msgs/SetLightProperties
    service, but that only changes a light element (illumination) -
    Gazebo Classic has no public API to change a spawned model's visual
    element material, which is what actually makes a lens look colored/lit.
    See limo_plugin/src/traffic_light_plugin.cpp for the approach that
    does work (publishing a full gazebo::msgs::Visual on the internal
    "~/visual" transport topic), adapted from SKKUAutoLab/
    H-Mobility-Autonomous-Advanced-Course-Simulation (GPL-2.0).
  </description>
</model>
